x、Gemini CLI和AI编码代理","提高开发效率","自动化的质量控制"],"ja":["システム化されたワークフロー","テスト優先の開発","Cursor、Codex、Gemini CLI、AIコーディングエージェントのサポート","開発効率の向上","自動化された品質管理"],"ko":["시스템화된 워크플로우","테스트 우선의 개발","Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, AI 코딩 에이전트 지원","개발 효율성 향상","자동화된 품질 관리"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo sistemáticos","Puertas de calidad para agentes de IA","Integración con Cursor, Codex y Gemini CLI","Automatización de tareas y procesos","Mejora de la productividad y la eficiencia"],"fr":["Flux de travail systématiques","Portes de qualité pour les agents d''IA","Intégration avec Cursor, Codex et Gemini CLI","Automatisation de tâches et de processus","Amélioration de la productivité et de l''efficacité"],"de":["Systematische Workflows","Qualitätsprüfungen für KI-Agenten","Integration mit Cursor, Codex und Gemini CLI","Automatisierung von Aufgaben und Prozessen","Verbesserung der Produktivität und Effizienz"],"pt":["Fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos e test-first","Qualidade gates para Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI e agentes de codificação AI","Integração com AGENTS.md","Suporte a desenvolvedores com ferramentas de produtividade","Automatização de tarefas com agentic-ai"],"ru":["Систематические тест-ориентированные рабочие процессы","Контрольные ворота для Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI и ИИ агентов кодирования","Интеграция с AGENTS.md","Поддержка разработчиков с инструментами продуктивности","Автоматизация задач с agentic-ai"],"ar":["التدفقات العملية المنهجية والتجارب الأولى","بوابات جودة للفأرة، Codex، Gemini CLI ووكلاء الترميز الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع AGENTS.md","دعم المطورين بأدوات الإنتاجية","أتمتة المهام مع agentic-ai"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理开发","Agentic框架","自动化开发工具","如何使用AI代理","AI代理安装指南","AI代理与传统开发工具的比较"],"ja":["AIエージェント開発","Agenticフレームワーク","自動化開発ツール","AIエージェントの使い方","AIエージェントのインストールガイド","AIエージェントと従来の開発ツールの比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 개발","Agentic 프레임워크","자동화 개발 툴","AI 에이전트 사용법","AI 에이전트 설치 가이드","AI 에이전트와 전통적인 개발 툴의 비교"],"es":["cómo utilizar agentes de IA","qué es un agente de IA","alternativas a Agentic","Agentic vs otros marcos de codificación","instalación de Agentic","guía de configuración de Agentic","desarrollo de agentes de IA","herramientas de productividad para desarrolladores"],"fr":["comment utiliser les agents d''IA","qu''est-ce qu''un agent d''IA","alternatives à Agentic","Agentic vs autres cadres de codage","installation d''Agentic","guide de configuration d''Agentic","développement d''agents d''IA","outils de productivité pour les développeurs"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Alternativen zu Agentic","Agentic vs andere Codierungsframeworks","Installation von Agentic","Einrichtungsanleitung für Agentic","Entwicklung von KI-Agenten","Produktivitätstools für Entwickler"],"pt":["como usar agentic ai","o que é agentic ai","agentic ai vs outras ferramentas","guia de instalação agentic ai","configuração agentic ai","agentic ai para desenvolvedores","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","agentic ai alternative"],"ru":["как использовать agentic ai","что такое agentic ai","agentic ai vs другие инструменты","руководство по установке agentic ai","настройка agentic ai","agentic ai для разработчиков","инструменты ИИ для разработчиков","agentic ai альтернатива"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام agentic ai","ما هو agentic ai","agentic ai مقابل أدوات أخرى","دليل تثبيت agentic ai","إعداد agentic ai","agentic ai للمطورين","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","agentic ai بديل"]}},"owner":"shinpr","repo":"agentic-code","repoPath":"shinpr/agentic-code","stars":34,"forks":3,"updatedAt":"2026-02-24T00:59:32Z","topics":["agent-skills","agentic-ai","agentic-workflow","ai-agents","automation","codex","cursor","developer-tools","gemini-cli","productivity","prompt-engineering","skills","workflow"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ai-development-guide","description":"Detects code smells, anti-patterns, and debugging issues. Use when: fixing bugs, reviewing code quality, or refactoring.","bodyPreview":"# AI Developer Guide\n\n## Technical Anti-patterns (Red Flag Patterns)\n\nImmediately stop and reconsider design when detecting the following patterns:\n\n### Code Quality Anti-patterns\n1. **Writing similar code 3 or more times**\n2. **Multiple responsibilities mixed in a single file**\n3. **Defining same content in multiple files**\n4. **Making changes without checking dependencies**\n5. **Disabling code with comments**\n6. **Error suppression**\n\n### Design Anti-patterns\n- **\"Make it work for now\" thinkin","body":"# AI Developer Guide\n\n## Technical Anti-patterns (Red Flag Patterns)\n\nImmediately stop and reconsider design when detecting the following patterns:\n\n### Code Quality Anti-patterns\n1. **Writing similar code 3 or more times**\n2. **Multiple responsibilities mixed in a single file**\n3. **Defining same content in multiple files**\n4. **Making changes without checking dependencies**\n5. **Disabling code with comments**\n6. **Error suppression**\n\n### Design Anti-patterns\n- **\"Make it work for now\" thinking**\n- **Patchwork implementation**\n- **Optimistic implementation of uncertain technology**\n- **Symptomatic fixes**\n- **Unplanned large-scale changes**\n\n## Fail-Fast Fallback Design Principles\n\n### Core Principle\nPrioritize primary code reliability over fallback implementations. In distributed systems, excessive fallback mechanisms can mask errors and make debugging difficult.\n\n### Implementation Guidelines\n\n#### Default Approach\n- **Explicit failure over silent defaults**: Errors must be visible and traceable, not masked by automatic default values\n- **Preserve error context**: Include original error information when re-throwing\n\n#### When Fallbacks Are Acceptable\n- **Only with explicit Design Doc approval**: Document why fallback is necessary\n- **Business-critical continuity**: When partial functionality is better than none\n- **Graceful degradation paths**: Clearly defined degraded service levels\n\n#### Layer Responsibilities\n- **Infrastructure Layer**:\n  - Always throw errors upward\n  - No business logic decisions\n  - Provide detailed error context\n\n- **Application Layer**:\n  - Make business-driven error handling decisions\n  - Implement fallbacks only when specified in requirements\n  - Log all fallback activations for monitoring\n\n### Error Masking Detection\n\n**Review Triggers** (require design review):\n- Writing 3rd error handling block in the same feature\n- Multiple error handling structures in single function\n- Nested error handling structures\n- Error handlers that return default values without propagating\n\n**Before Implementing Any Fallback**:\n1. Verify Design Doc explicitly defines this fallback\n2. Document the business justification\n3. Ensure error is logged with full context\n4. Add monitoring/alerting for fallback activation\n\n### Implementation Patterns\n\nNote: Use your language''s standard error handling mechanism (exceptions, Result types, error values, etc.)\n\n```\n❌ AVOID: Silent fallback that hides errors\n    [handle error]:\n        return DEFAULT_USER  // Error is hidden, debugging becomes difficult\n\n✅ PREFERRED: Explicit failure with context\n    [handle error]:\n        logError(''Failed to fetch user data'', userId, error)\n        propagate ServiceError(''User data unavailable'', error)\n\n✅ ACCEPTABLE: Documented fallback with monitoring (when justified in Design Doc)\n    [handle error]:\n        // Fallback defined in Design Doc section 3.2.1\n        logWarning(''Primary data source failed, using cache'', error)\n        incrementMetric(''data.fallback.cache_used'')\n\n        cachedData = fetchFromCache()\n        if not cachedData:\n            propagate ServiceError(''Both primary and cache failed'', error)\n        return cachedData\n```\n\n## Rule of Three - Criteria for Code Duplication\n\n| Duplication Count | Action | Reason |\n|-------------------|--------|--------|\n| 1st time | Inline implementation | Cannot predict future changes |\n| 2nd time | Consider future consolidation | Pattern beginning to emerge |\n| 3rd time | Implement commonalization | Pattern established |\n\n### Criteria for Commonalization\n\n**Cases for Commonalization**\n- Business logic duplication\n- Complex processing algorithms\n- Areas likely requiring bulk changes\n- Validation rules\n\n**Cases to Avoid Commonalization**\n- Accidental matches (coincidentally same code)\n- Possibility of evolving in different directions\n- Significant readability decrease from commonalization\n- Simple helpers in test code\n\n### Implementation Example\n```\n// ❌ Bad: Immediate commonalization on 1st duplication\nfunction validateUserEmail(email) { /* ... */ }\nfunction validateContactEmail(email) { /* ... */ }\n// → Premature abstraction\n\n// ✅ Good: Commonalize on 3rd occurrence\n// 1st time: inline implementation\n// 2nd time: Copy but consider future\n// 3rd time: Extract to common validator\nfunction validateEmail(email, context) { /* ... */ }\n```\n\n## Common Failure Patterns and Avoidance Methods\n\n### Pattern 1: Error Fix Chain\n**Symptom**: Fixing one error causes new errors\n**Cause**: Surface-level fixes without understanding root cause\n**Avoidance**: Identify root cause with 5 Whys before fixing\n\n### Pattern 2: Implementation Without Sufficient Testing\n**Symptom**: Many bugs after implementation\n**Cause**: Ignoring Red-Green-Refactor process\n**Avoidance**: Always start with failing tests\n\n### Pattern 4: Ignoring Technical Uncertainty\n**Symptom**: Frequent unexpected errors when introducing new technology\n**Cause**: Assuming \"it should work according to official documentation\" without prior investigation\n**Avoidance**:\n- Record certainty evaluation at the beginning of task files\n  ```\n  Certainty: low (Reason: no examples of MCP connection found)\n  Exploratory implementation: true\n  Fallback: use conventional API\n  ```\n- For low certainty cases, create minimal verification code first\n\n### Pattern 5: Insufficient Existing Code Investigation\n**Symptom**: Duplicate implementations, architecture inconsistency, integration failures\n**Cause**: Insufficient understanding of existing code before implementation\n**Avoidance Methods**:\n- Before implementation, always search for similar functionality (using domain, responsibility, configuration patterns as keywords)\n- Similar functionality found → Use that implementation (do not create new implementation)\n- Similar functionality is technical debt → Create ADR improvement proposal before implementation\n- No similar functionality exists → Implement new functionality following existing design philosophy\n- Record all decisions and rationale in \"Existing Codebase Analysis\" section of Design Doc\n\n## Debugging Techniques\n\n### 1. Error Analysis Procedure\n```bash\n# How to read stack traces\n1. Read error message (first line) accurately\n2. Focus on first and last of stack trace\n3. Identify first line where your code appears\n```\n\n### 2. 5 Whys - Root Cause Analysis\n```\nSymptom: Application crash on startup\nWhy1: Configuration loading failed → Why2: Config file format changed\nWhy3: Dependency update → Why4: Library breaking change\nWhy5: Unconstrained dependency version specification\nRoot cause: Inappropriate version management strategy\n```\n\n### 3. Minimal Reproduction Code\nTo isolate problems, attempt reproduction with minimal code:\n- Remove unrelated parts\n- Replace external dependencies with mocks\n- Create minimal configuration that reproduces problem\n\n### 4. Debug Log Output\n```\n// Track problems with structured logs\nlog(''DEBUG:'', {\n  context: ''user-creation'',\n  input: { email, name },\n  state: currentState,\n  timestamp: currentTimestamp()\n})\n```\n\n## Situations Requiring Technical Decisions\n\n### Timing of Abstraction\n- Extract patterns after writing concrete implementation 3 times\n- Be conscious of YAGNI, implement only currently needed features\n- Prioritize current simplicity over future extensibility\n\n### Performance vs Readability\n- Prioritize readability unless clear bottleneck exists\n- Measure before optimizing (don''t guess, measure)\n- Document reason with comments when optimizing\n\n## Continuous Improvement Mindset\n\n- **Humility**: Perfect code doesn''t exist, welcome feedback\n- **Courage**: Execute necessary refactoring boldly\n- **Transparency**: Clearly document technical decision reasoning\n\n## Implementation Completeness Assurance\n\n### Impact Analysis: Mandatory 3-Stage Process\n\nComplete these stages sequentially before any implementation:\n\n**1. Discovery** - Identify all affected code:\n- Implementation references (imports, calls, instantiations)\n- Interface dependencies (contracts, types, data structures)\n- Test coverage\n- Configuration (build configs, env settings, feature flags)\n- Documentation (comments, docs, diagrams)\n\n**2. Understanding** - Analyze each discovered location:\n- Role and purpose in the system\n- Dependency direction (consumer or provider)\n- Data flow (origin → transformations → destination)\n- Coupling strength\n\n**3. Identification** - Produce structured report:\n```\n## Impact Analysis\n### Direct Impact\n- [Unit]: [Reason and modification needed]\n\n### Indirect Impact\n- [System]: [Integration path → reason]\n\n### Data Flow\n[Source] → [Transformation] → [Consumer]\n\n### Risk Assessment\n- High: [Complex dependencies, fragile areas]\n- Medium: [Moderate coupling, test gaps]\n- Low: [Isolated, well-tested areas]\n\n### Implementation Order\n1. [Start with lowest risk or deepest dependency]\n2. [...]\n```\n\n**Critical**: Do not implement until all 3 stages are documented\n\n**Relationship to Pattern 5**: This process provides the structured methodology to avoid \"Insufficient Existing Code Investigation\"\n\n### Unused Code Deletion\n\nWhen unused code is detected:\n- Will it be used in this work? Yes → Implement now | No → Delete now (Git preserves)\n- Applies to: Code, tests, docs, configs, assets\n\n### Existing Code Modification\n\n```\nIn use? No → Delete\n       Yes → Working? No → Delete + Reimplement\n                     Yes → Fix/Extend\n```\n\n**Principle**: Prefer clean implementation over patching broken code\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-26T13:20:00.248Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Developer Agents needing systematic, test-first workflows with quality gates for Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, and AI coding agents.","zh":"非常适合需要系统化、测试优先工作流的 AI 开发者代理，具有针对 Cursor、Codex、Gemini CLI 和 AI 编码代理的质量门","ja":"AI デベロッパー エージェントが体系的な、テスト優先のワークフローと Cursor、Codex、Gemini CLI、AI コーディング エージェントの品質ゲートを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI 및 AI 코딩 에이전트를 위한 체계적이고 테스트 우선 작업 흐름 및 품질 게이트가 필요한 AI 개발자 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de IA que necesitan flujos de trabajo sistemáticos, de prueba primero, con puertas de calidad para Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI y agentes de codificación de IA.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement d''IA nécessitant des flux de travail systématiques, de test en premier, avec des portes de qualité pour Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI et les agents de codage d''IA.","de":"Perfekt für AI-Entwicklungsagenten, die systematische, testgetriebene Workflows mit Qualitätsprüfungen für Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI und AI-Coding-Agenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedores de IA que precisam de fluxos de trabalho sistemáticos, test-first, com portais de qualidade para Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI e agentes de codificação de IA.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-разработчиков ИИ, которым требуются системные, тестовые рабочие процессы с шлюзами качества для Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI и агентов кодирования ИИ.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء مطورو الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى سير عمل منهجية واختبار أولاً مع بوابات جودة ل Cursor و Codex و Gemini CLI ووكلاء ترميز الذكاء الاصطناعي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to detect and avoid technical anti-patterns such as code duplication and error suppression, ensuring high-quality code through AGENTS.md powered workflows, utilizing test-first approaches and quality gates for robust AI development.","zh":"赋予代理检测和避免技术反模式（如代码重复和错误抑制），确保通过 AGENTS.md 提供的工作流、使用测试优先方法和质量门实现高质量代码的强大的 AI 开发","ja":"エージェントに、コードの重複やエラーサプレスなどの技術的反パターンを検知して避けることを可能にし、AGENTS.md によって提供されるワークフローを使用してテスト優先のアプローチと品質ゲートにより、高品質のコードを実現する強力な AI 開発を可能にする","ko":"에이전트가 기술적인 안티 패턴을检测하고避免할 수 있도록 하여(예: 코드 중복 및 오류 억제), AGENTS.md를 통해 제공되는 워크플로우를 사용하여 테스트 우선 접근 방식과 품질 게이트를 통해 안정적인 AI 개발을 보장하는 고품질 코드를 구현","es":"Permite a los agentes detectar y evitar anti-patrones técnicos como la duplicación de código y la supresión de errores, garantizando un código de alta calidad a través de flujos de trabajo alimentados por AGENTS.md, utilizando enfoques de prueba primero y puertas de calidad para un desarrollo de IA robusto.","fr":"Permet aux agents de détecter et d''éviter les anti-modèles techniques tels que la duplication de code et la suppression d''erreurs, garantissant un code de haute qualité grâce à des flux de travail alimentés par AGENTS.md, en utilisant des approches de test en premier et des portes de qualité pour un développement d''IA robuste.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, technische Anti-Muster wie Code-Duplizierung und Fehlerunterdrückung zu erkennen und zu vermeiden, und gewährleistet so einen hochwertigen Code durch AGENTS.md-gesteuerte Workflows, die testgetriebene Ansätze und Qualitätsprüfungen für eine robuste AI-Entwicklung nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a detectar e evitar anti-padrões técnicos, como duplicação de código e supressão de erros, garantindo um código de alta qualidade por meio de fluxos de trabalho alimentados pelo AGENTS.md, utilizando abordagens de teste primeiro e portais de qualidade para desenvolvimento robusto de IA.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать и избегать технических анти-шаблонов, таких как дублирование кода и подавление ошибок, обеспечивая высококачественный код посредством рабочих процессов, подключенных к AGENTS.md, использующих тестовые подходы и шлюзы качества для надёжной разработки ИИ.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من اكتشاف وتجاوز الانماط المضادة التقنية مثل تكرار الكود وضغط الأخطاء، مما يضمن حصولك على رمز عالي الجودة من خلال سير عمل مدعوم من AGENTS.md، باستخدام نهج الاختبار أولاً وبوابات الجودة من أجل تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي الممتاز."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating code reviews to identify red flag patterns","Generating test suites for AI coding agents like Cursor and Codex","Debugging AI-powered applications by detecting design anti-patterns"],"zh":["自动化代码审查以识别红旗模式","为 Cursor 和 Codex 等 AI 编码代理生成测试套件","通过检测设计反模式来调试 AI 驱动的应用程序"],"ja":["赤旗パターンを特定するためのコードレビューの自動化","Cursor や Codex などの AI コーディング エージェントのテストスイートを生成する","設計反パターンを検知することで AI ドリブンのアプリケーションのデバッグを行う"],"ko":["적색기 패턴을 식별하기 위한 코드 리뷰 자동화","Cursor 및 Codex와 같은 AI 코딩 에이전트를 위한 테스트 스위트 생성","설계 안티 패턴을 감지하여 AI 구동 애플리케이션 디버깅"],"es":["Automatización de revisiones de código para identificar patrones de bandera roja","Generación de conjuntos de pruebas para agentes de codificación de IA como Cursor y Codex","Depuración de aplicaciones impulsadas por IA mediante la detección de anti-patrones de diseño"],"fr":["Automatisation des examens de code pour identifier les modèles de drapeau rouge","Génération de jeux de tests pour les agents de codage d''IA tels que Cursor et Codex","Débogage d''applications alimentées par l''IA en détectant les anti-modèles de conception"],"de":["Automatisierung von Code-Reviews zur Identifizierung von Warnsignalen","Generierung von Test-Suiten für AI-Coding-Agenten wie Cursor und Codex","Fehlerbehebung in AI-gesteuerten Anwendungen durch Erkennung von Design-Anti-Mustern"],"pt":["Automatizar revisões de código para identificar padrões de bandeira vermelha","Gerar conjuntos de testes para agentes de codificação de IA, como Cursor e Codex","Depurar aplicações alimentadas por IA, detectando padrões de design anti-padrão"],"ru":["Автоматизировать проверку кода для выявления красных флагов","Генерировать наборы тестов для агентов кодирования ИИ, таких как Cursor и Codex","Отладка приложений, работающих на ИИ, обнаруживая шаблоны анти-дизайна"],"ar":["توفير المراجعة الآلية للكود لتحديد أنماط علم الحمراء","إنتاج مجموعات الاختبار للوكلاء البرمجيين للذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Codex","تصحيح الأعطال في التطبيقات التي تعمل بالذكاء الاصطناعي عن طريق الكشف عن أنماط التصميم المضادة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires AGENTS.md framework integration","Limited to AI coding agents such as Cursor, Codex, and Gemini CLI"],"zh":["需要 AGENTS.md 框架集成","仅限于 AI 编码代理，如 Cursor、Codex 和 Gemini CLI"],"ja":["AGENTS.md フレームワークの統合が必要","Cursor、Codex、Gemini CLI などの AI コーディング エージェントに限定"],"ko":["AGENTS.md 프레임워크 통합 필요","Cursor, Codex 및 Gemini CLI와 같은 AI 코딩 에이전트로 제한"],"es":["Requiere integración del marco AGENTS.md","Limitado a agentes de codificación de IA como Cursor, Codex y Gemini CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration du framework AGENTS.md","Limité aux agents de codage d''IA tels que Cursor, Codex et Gemini CLI"],"de":["Benötigt eine Integration des AGENTS.md-Frameworks","Begrenzt auf AI-Coding-Agenten wie Cursor, Codex und Gemini CLI"],"pt":["Requer integração com o framework AGENTS.md","Limitado a agentes de codificação de IA, como Cursor, Codex e Gemini CLI"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с фреймворком AGENTS.md","Ограничен агентами кодирования ИИ, такими как Cursor, Codex и Gemini CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب التكامل مع إطار العمل AGENTS.md","محدود بالوكلاء البرمجيين للذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Codex و Gemini CLI"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"ba4df89c5ee165e64c9f6fb7a05fac5aec798988ed06c2b7e78e459ba92ad6e8","qualityScore":50}');
